      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) فِي قَوْلِ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ وَ أَنْزَلْنا مِنَ السَّماءِ ماءً بِقَدَرٍ فَأَسْكَنَّاهُ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَ إِنَّا عَلى ذَهابٍ بِهِ لَقادِرُونَ فَقَالَ يَعْنِي مَاءَ الْعَقِيقِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "From him, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Al Abbas Bin Marouf, from Al Nowfaly from Al Yaqouby, from Isa Bin Abdullah, from Suleyman Bin Ja’far having said: ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> said regarding the Words of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:23#h18\"><a href=\"/books/quran:23#h18\">[23:18]</a></a> And We send down water from the sky according to a measure, then We Settle it in the earth, and We are able to Take it away</span>. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Meaning the water of the ravines’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. It is narrated from the narrator of the previous Hadith from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from al-‘Abbas ibn Ma’ruf from Nawfaliy from al-Ya‘qubiy from “Isa ibn ‘Abd Allah from Sulayman ibn Ja‘far who has said the following: “About the meaning of the words of Allah, most Majestic, most Glorious, ‘We sent water from the sky in measures and placed it on earth and We have the power to take it away,’ <a href=\"/#/books/quran:23#h18\"><a href=\"/books/quran:23#h18\">[23:18]</a></a> abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘It means canyons and ravines.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
